           'The ending changes an operating eligibility rule: Earth’s residents become recognized citizens, a child receives treatment, and medical ships deploy automatically to people now classified as needing care. This makes advanced treatment independent of the earlier citizenship exclusion and ordinary ability to pay. It is a realized sectoral transition in access to an essential service, not merely a speech promising future reform.\n\nThe guarantee score improves access to care for the newly included population but stays moderate because the film does not redistribute food, homes or all income. The output still comes from concentrated infrastructure, and a software reset does not establish equal resident ownership. Automatic dispatch also does not prove an independent AI government. Human industrial and care work outside this system can continue, so no sudden nonworking percentage follows from the legal change. The record describes the functioning protocol at the ending; its later capacity, durability under political opposition and wider economic effects remain unverified.',
