           'The Eternals have a continuing technological support arrangement: the Tabernacle restores their bodies after death, while even punished Renegades receive food. This creates a limited, privileged provision enclave with automatic life maintenance. It rests partly on coercion outside the enclave, since Brutals supply grain through forced farming. The record does not turn that human labor into automation or describe all humanity as post-work.\n\nGuarantees are qualified by compulsory immortality and punitive aging, which can withdraw health even while support continues. Productive control is harder to place: Eternals vote and exercise power over outsiders, yet the Tabernacle constrains their own continued existence. The short sources do not resolve that division well enough for a control coordinate. An AI-support regime is therefore provisional, with human-control alternatives. Stewardship of knowledge, breadmaking and other useful activity remain work; immortality and boredom do not establish a nonworking percentage. The later destruction of the system and the mortal life that follows are separate arrangements.',
           {'guarantees': -0.5, 'control': None, 'nonworking': None},
